# Box-wide tool credentials, sourced by every shell (~/.bashrc.d/devbox.sh).
# Bootstrap installs this template as ~/.config/devbox/secrets.env at mode 600
# and never fills it; it lives on the bind mount, so it survives every rebuild.
#
# Plain KEY=value pairs only - no `export`, no `op://` references. The container
# holds no 1Password account by design (docs/secrets.md): render values on the
# laptop, where approving access is yours to do, and copy them in.
#
# What belongs here: credentials every project shares, i.e. the tools' own.
# What does not: anything a single project needs. Project secrets go in that
# project's .env so a leak stays scoped to one project - GCP included, since
# each project has its own GCP project and therefore its own ADC key path.

# GitHub CLI, one token per account. The working directory picks which one is
# used, on the same rule git uses for identities: ~/projects/work/** is
# work, everything else personal (`devbox-gh-token --account` reports it).
#
# Keep both fine-grained, expiring and read-mostly: contents/actions/checks read
# for dashboards and pipelines, issues or pull-requests write only if agents
# should post. `git push` never needs either - that goes over SSH.
#
# Unlike the rest of this file, these two are read by `devbox-gh-token` directly
# as well as through the shell, so a new token works without reconnecting.
#
# Do NOT define a plain GH_TOKEN here: it overrides both and disables the
# per-directory choice for every tree. For a one-off, pass it per command
# instead: GH_TOKEN=<other> gh ...
# GH_TOKEN_PERSONAL=github_pat_...
# GH_TOKEN_WORK=github_pat_...

# Models used by OMP itself, as opposed to a project's own LLM calls.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
